---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pricing" description="AMI pricing for Navigation and Precision Calibration. 14-day free trial on both plans." lang="en">
  <section class="section hero compact-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
    <h1>Metabolic navigation, starting at $19.</h1>
    <p class="lede">AMI turns metabolic signals into clear daily decisions. Start with Navigation, then use Precision Calibration when deeper data can sharpen the route. Both plans include a 14-day free trial.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={site.playStoreUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start 14-day free trial</a><a class="button secondary" href="/ami/experience">See AMI in action</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid two">
    <article class="card highlight"><p class="eyebrow">AMI Navigation</p><h2>$19 / month</h2><p>Daily metabolic decision support for fasting windows, signals, coach guidance, and route continuity.</p><div class="compare"><div class="compare-row"><div>Best for</div><div>Daily direction and consistency.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Includes</div><div>Coach, fasting route, daily metrics, and route state.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Trial</div><div>14-day free trial.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Labs</div><div>Can inform the route while Precision Calibration keeps deeper observability organized.</div></div></div></article>
    <article class="card blue-card"><p class="eyebrow">AMI Precision Calibration</p><h2>$49 / month</h2><p>Deeper observability when labs, ratios, longitudinal recalibration, and precision review matter.</p><div class="compare"><div class="compare-row"><div>Best for</div><div>Fine-tuning with deeper data.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Includes</div><div>Labs, ratios, trends, calibration context, and precision dashboards.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Trial</div><div>14-day free trial.</div></div><div class="compare-row"><div>Cycle</div><div>Use it when it matters, then return to Navigation with a sharper route.</div></div></div></article>
  </section>

  <section class="section card highlight"><p class="eyebrow">The AMI cycle</p><h2>Navigate. Calibrate. Navigate again.</h2><p>Most days need a clearer next decision. New data sharpens the route when it matters. When new labs or a deeper question appear, Precision Calibration sharpens the route. Then Navigation keeps the route alive.</p><div class="cycle"><span>Navigation</span><strong>-></strong><span>Precision Calibration</span><strong>-></strong><span>Sharper Navigation</span></div></section>

  <section class="section grid"><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Decision cycle</p><h2>Two modes, one system.</h2><p>Navigation and Precision Calibration are states in the same metabolic engineering loop.</p></article><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Transparent</p><h2>Start simple.</h2><p>Begin with daily route support. Calibrate when more precision is useful.</p></article><article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Boundaries</p><h2>Engineering for metabolic navigation.</h2><p>AMI supports metabolic navigation and personal optimization with clear wellness boundaries; it does not diagnose, prevent, treat, or cure disease.</p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
